        }
      ],
      "extract": "In this section, we show an asymptotic formula of the divergent series ${}_1\\psi_0(a;-;q,x)$. At first, we review Ramanujan's sum for ${}_1\\psi_1(a;b;q,z)$ and its property. Ramanujan gives the following sum [@Hardy] $${}_1\\psi_1(a;b;q,z)=\\frac{(q,b/a,az,q/az;q)_\\infty}{(b,q/a,z,b/az;q)_\\infty},\\qquad \\left|b/a\\right|<|z|<1. \\label{Rsum}$$ We can regard this sum as a $q$-analogue of the bilateral binomial theorem",
      "extractCut": true
    },
